0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","$L2","2.11",{"topic":{"id":"2.11","title":"Documentation and Reporting of Digital Evidence","minutes":12,"summary":"Write a report that lets a reader trace every conclusion back to an exhibit and reproduce the important examination steps.","sections":[{"title":"Structure for the reader","body":["Begin with the instruction, scope, examiner, dates, exhibit list, and question. Summarize findings without overstating them. Follow with the environment, methods, tools and versions, relevant settings, analysis, limitations, and conclusions. Put hashes, acquisition logs, custody records, and detailed timelines in appendices so that the main narrative remains readable.","Give every exhibit a stable identifier and connect it to its source. Describe what was examined, not only what was found. If a tool produced thousands of results, explain the selection criteria and whether material contrary to the hypothesis was considered. An expert report should help the court evaluate the evidence, not advertise the examiner or the software."]},{"title":"Reproducibility and transformations","body":["Record time-zone normalization, clock offsets, decoding methods, search expressions, and relevant tool defaults. A timestamp shown in local time may differ from the underlying UTC record. A converted image or redacted excerpt is a new output; preserve its relationship to the original. Explain any error messages and whether they affect the relied-on result.","Separate observations from interpretations in the wording. “The log contains event ID 4624 at this time” is not equivalent to “the accused personally logged in”. Explain the event’s semantics, account type, and limitations. Where a second tool corroborates a result, describe what each actually verified rather than merely listing two product names."]},{"title":"Review, disclosure, and presentation","body":["Use technical review to check calculations, exhibit references, and the logic of conclusions. A reviewer should identify unsupported leaps, inconsistent timestamps, and missing limitations. Maintain version control and preserve the underlying notes needed to explain the report. Follow applicable disclosure obligations rather than selectively presenting only supportive artifacts.","A clear visual timeline can help a non-technical reader, but every item should point back to a source. Avoid inflammatory labels and unnecessary personal data. If new evidence changes the conclusion, issue a transparent correction or supplement. Professional credibility depends on being willing to revise an opinion when the evidence changes."]}],"practice":{"title":"Repair an unsupported finding","scenario":"A draft says: “The suspect deleted the invoice at 22:10, proving fraud.” The only source is a file deletion timestamp.","steps":["Rewrite the observation without naming an actor.","Check the clock, filesystem semantics, and possible automated cleanup.","Identify evidence needed for attribution and intent.","Add a source-linked timeline and explicit limitations."],"debrief":"A careful report can be both clear and cautious. It does not turn a filesystem event into proof of a person’s state of mind."},"terms":[],"lawIds":["bsa","bnss"],"sources":["bsa","cert","nist-guide"],"labId":"certificate","unit":2,"objectives":["Explain structure for the reader and apply it to an investigation.","Explain reproducibility and transformations and apply it to an investigation.","Explain review, disclosure, and presentation and apply it to an investigation."],"question":{"id":"q-2.11","prompt":"Which statement is suitable for an expert report without further evidence?","options":["The suspect is definitely guilty.","The recovered file’s timestamp is 22:10 UTC; attribution requires further evidence.","Everyone using this software commits fraud.","The tool is popular, so its output needs no explanation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"The report should distinguish the recorded artifact from conclusions about identity, intent, and criminal liability.","unit":2}}}]],["$L3"],"$L4"]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"mMiCr23A_-Cpk0hZkfT7X"}
